---
title: Potato and Onion Grills with Olives
servings: 6
course: Main
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
---

Put the @potatoes{675%g}(thinly sliced) and @onion{1%large}(thinly sliced) into a large bowl. Whisk together the @olive oil{3%tbsp} and @white wine vinegar{1%tbsp}, drizzle over the potato mixture and toss well. Add the @thyme leaves or chopped fresh rosemary{3%tbsp}, season with @salt and @black pepper{}(freshly ground), then toss again until evenly coated.

Divide the mixture among six large squares of thick foil. Slice the @stoned black olives{16} into thin rings and scatter them over the top.

Close the parcels, securing the seams well. Cook over a medium heat for about ~{30%minutes}, turning the parcels occasionally, or until the potatoes are tender.